flowchart TB
accTitle: Learning and freezing a tokenizer
accDescr: Select a representative sample from a curated corpus. Configure normalization, pre-token boundaries, alphabet and special tokens. Train vocabulary and segmentation rules. Evaluate held-out coverage and fidelity, revise when needed, and freeze a versioned tokenizer artifact. This is distinct from training neural language-model weights.
 A["Curated text corpus"] --> B["Choose a representative sample<br/>Language and domain mixture"]
 B --> C["Configure the text pipeline<br/>Optional normalization; pre-tokenization<br/>Alphabet and special-token policy"]
 C --> D["Learn the tokenizer<br/>BPE merges or Unigram vocabulary / scores"]
 D --> E["Evaluate on held-out text<br/>Compression, coverage, round trips"]
 E -. "Revise design if needed" .-> C
 E --> F["Freeze the complete tokenizer<br/>Rules, vocabulary, decoder, configuration"]
 class A source;
 class B corpus;
 class C,D,E learning;
 class F output;

classDef source fill:#edf1f5,stroke:#8495a5,color:#202b38;
classDef corpus fill:#e8f0fa,stroke:#386998,color:#142e4b;
classDef learning fill:#fff3da,stroke:#aa7a25,color:#583b0e;
classDef encoding fill:#e7f3ee,stroke:#3c7e66,color:#173e30;
classDef output fill:#ffffff,stroke:#386998,stroke-width:2px,color:#142e4b;
